{
	//  PETPORTS -- POLYMORPHIC ITEMS
	//
	//  ONE ITEM NAME, MANY GENUINELY DIFFERENT ITEMS.
	//
	//  Most items are what their name says. A few are a FAMILY behind a single
	//  name, with the actual identity living in the descriptor's parameters --
	//  every Betabound music sheet is `sb_musicsheet` and differs only by which
	//  song it holds. Dyed clothing is the vanilla version of the same idea,
	//  though there the base name still describes the thing.
	//
	//  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The restock beacon stores a request as a NAME, so a
	//  request for `sb_musicsheet` means ANY music sheet -- which is the right
	//  behaviour and the only one that keeps petports_filterAccepts a pure
	//  function of a name. The problem is purely what to CALL it in the pane.
	//
	//  root.itemConfig is handed a bare descriptor, with no parameters and no
	//  seed, so a generated item re-runs its build script with a fresh random
	//  seed every call. For a music sheet that means the pane names one
	//  arbitrary song -- actively misleading, because the request is not for
	//  that song. A stable family name is both honest and more useful.
	//
	//  A NAME HERE IS A DISPLAY OVERRIDE AND NOTHING ELSE. It changes no
	//  matching, no counting, no eviction. If it did, it would be a second
	//  vocabulary competing with the filter manifest.
	//
	//  FOR MODDERS: patch /displayNames/<itemName> with the string you want the
	//  request list to show. Name the FAMILY, not an example of it, and say
	//  whose it is -- a player with forty mods installed needs to know which one
	//  put it in their storage.
	//
	//  ABOUT THIRTY CHARACTERS FIT IN A REQUEST ROW. Past that it is trimmed
	//  with a trailing "..", which breaks nothing but reads worse than a name
	//  chosen to fit. Both entries below are comfortably inside it.
	//
	//  The two entries below are Betabound's, and they are here because
	//  Betabound is prolific enough that its two most storage-fragmenting drops
	//  are worth supporting out of the box. Neither this mod nor Betabound
	//  depends on the other: an entry for an item the game does not have is
	//  simply never looked up.
	"displayNames" : {
		"sb_musicsheet" : "Music Sheets (Betabound!)",
		"sb_blueprint" : "Blueprints (Betabound!)"
	}
}
